{"compatibility":"as-is","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: as-is.

Protected data: `x1`, `y1`, and `x2`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

No changes were required. Each protected observation is a top-level data variable and is observed exactly once with a plain built-in sampling statement. Parameter priors are built-in sampling statements and occur before parameter use. The context input `N` is not protected.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=1> N;
  vector[N] x1; // Complete observation
  vector[N] y1; // Complete observation
  vector[N] x2; // Incomplete observation
}

parameters {
  real mu1;
  real<lower=0> tau1;

  real mu2;
  real<lower=0> tau2;

  real<lower=0> sigma;
}

model {
  mu1 ~ normal(0, 3);
  tau1 ~ normal(0, 1);

  mu2 ~ normal(0, 3);
  tau2 ~ normal(0, 1);

  sigma ~ normal(0, 1);

  x1 ~ normal(mu1, tau1);
  y1 ~ normal(x1, sigma);

  x2 ~ normal(mu2, tau2);
}

generated quantities {
  // Predict completion of second observation
  array[N] real y2_pred = normal_rng(x2, sigma);
}
